{"value":{"@ir":{"@type":"Document","blocks":[{"@type":"Heading","appendix":false,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"Introduction"}],"label":null,"level":1,"numbered":true,"part":false},{"@type":"Paragraph","align":null,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"A popular tool for evaluating generative models is the classifier two-sample test (C2ST). It reframes distributional comparison between "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"p(x)"},{"@type":"Text","value":" and "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"q(x)"},{"@type":"Text","value":" as a classification task over the space "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\mathcal{X}"},{"@type":"Text","value":", with the Bayes-optimal classifier bisecting "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}"},{"@type":"Text","value":" between the two means."}]},{"@type":"Heading","appendix":false,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"Summary of contributions."}],"label":null,"level":4,"numbered":false,"part":false},{"@type":"Paragraph","align":null,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"We introduce the Conformal C2ST and give a robustness theory for weak classifiers. We show that conformal calibration decouples type-I error control from discriminative accuracy."}]},{"@type":"Heading","appendix":false,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"A toy example."}],"label":null,"level":4,"numbered":false,"part":false},{"@type":"Paragraph","align":null,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"Consider "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\mathcal{N}(\\mathbf{0},{I}_{2})"},{"@type":"Text","value":" versus a mean shift, so that "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"q"},{"@type":"Text","value":" is "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\mathcal{N}([0.5,0{]}^{\\top },{I}_{2})"},{"@type":"Text","value":". The rank statistic"}]},{"@type":"MathBlock","env":"displaymath","label":null,"latex":"r=\\sum _{i=1}^{M}\\mathbb{I}\\lbrace \\theta \\leq {\\tilde{\\theta }}_{i}\\rbrace","line_labels":[],"numbered":false},{"@type":"Paragraph","align":null,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"is uniform over "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\lbrace 0,1,\\dots ,M\\rbrace"},{"@type":"Text","value":" when "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"q"},{"@type":"Text","value":" matches "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"p"},{"@type":"Text","value":"."}]},{"@type":"Heading","appendix":false,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"Robustness of the uniform test"}],"label":null,"level":1,"numbered":true,"part":false},{"@type":"Paragraph","align":null,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"Let "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\mathcal{O}"},{"@type":"Text","value":" denote an oracle and write the conformal "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"p"},{"@type":"Text","value":"-value as a function of the score. We control the variance "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"Var[r]"},{"@type":"Text","value":" and the expectation "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\mathbb{E}[r]"},{"@type":"Text","value":" of the rank statistic under the null."}]},{"@type":"Theorem","blocks":[{"@type":"Paragraph","align":null,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"For any plug-in classifier with score "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"s"},{"@type":"Text","value":", the conformal calibration map satisfies"}]}],"counter":null,"kind":"Theorem","label":null,"title":[{"@type":"Text","value":"Decoupling"}]},{"@type":"MathBlock","env":"displaymath","label":null,"latex":"\\vert \\mathbb{E}[\\phi (s)]-\\alpha \\vert \\leq \\left| s-{s}^{\\star } \\right|{\\rightarrow }^{ n\\rightarrow \\infty  }0,","line_labels":[],"numbered":false},{"@type":"Paragraph","align":null,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"where "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"{s}^{\\star }"},{"@type":"Text","value":" is the Bayes-optimal score and "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\left| \\alpha  \\right|\\leq 1"},{"@type":"Text","value":"."}]},{"@type":"Paragraph","align":null,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"As shown in Theorem "},{"@type":"Ref","bookmark":null,"key":"thm:decouple","ref_kind":"generic","style":"plain"},{"@type":"Text","value":", the conformal test maintains validity even when the classifier is weak, since the ranking signal "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\begin{matrix} rank \\\\ \\longrightarrow  \\end{matrix}"},{"@type":"Text","value":" aggregates across draws."}]}],"book":false,"labels":{},"meta":{"@type":"DocumentMeta","abstract":[{"@type":"Paragraph","align":null,"inlines":[{"@type":"Text","value":"We study the "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\mathcal{M}"},{"@type":"Text","value":"-closed validation of a generative model "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"q"},{"@type":"Text","value":" against a target "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"p"},{"@type":"Text","value":" over the space "},{"@type":"Math","latex":"\\mathcal{X}"},{"@type":"Text","value":". Conformal calibration turns a weak plug-in classifier into a powerful two-sample test with finite-sample type-I control."}]}],"affiliations":[],"authors":[[{"@type":"Text","value":"UAT Fixture"}],[{"@type":"Text","value":"January 2, 2026"}]],"cjk_main_font":null,"cjk_mono_font":null,"cjk_sans_font":null,"columns":1,"date":null,"keywords":null,"language":null,"main_font":null,"running_head":null,"title":[{"@type":"Text","value":"The Conformal Classifier Two-Sample Test"}]}}}}
